He was born into the noble Sakyan lineage. That is why the multitude of people offer such great honor and respect—thus one heretical teacher presented his view. Then, another heretical teacher spoke his opinion, saying: At the time of the birth of the Monk Gotama, many wonderful and extraordinary phenomena occurred; that is why the multitude of people offer such great honor and respect. Likewise:

When the newborn was brought to pay homage to the hermit Devila, King Suddhodhana, the father, joined his two hands and moved the child toward the hermit Devila, but miraculously, the child's feet spontaneously rose and rested upon the matted hair of the hermit Devila’s head;

When the plowing festival was held, the Great Being was placed to sleep under the shade of a rose-apple tree, and while the shadows of other trees shifted according to the movement of the sun, the shade of the rose-apple tree where the Great Being lay remained unchanged even in the afternoon;

Because he is exceedingly beautiful in appearance;

Because, upon seeing the four great omens, he was deeply moved by spiritual urgency (saṃvega) and renounced the glory of a Universal Monarch (Cakkavatti) that was about to reach his hands to become a monk—it is for these reasons that the multitude of people offer such great honor and respect.

